WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:07.120
After being cancelled after only three seasons,&nbsp;
fan outcry led to “Longmire” being rescued by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:13.040
Netflix for another three seasons. But now that&nbsp;
it’s over, are you longing for more "Longmire?"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:18.560
These 15 shows will fill the neo-Western hole&nbsp;
in your heart left behind by the beloved series.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.880
Amazon Prime's "Bosch" is the perfect example&nbsp;
of a show that captures the vibe of "Longmire"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.760
without sharing its Western setting.&nbsp;
The series stars Titus Welliver,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:36.480
who sci-fi fans may know as the Man in Black from&nbsp;
"Lost," as Los Angeles detective Harry Bosch. Not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.680
unlike "Longmire," the series is based on a&nbsp;
set of novels written by Michael Connelly.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:47.280
This procedural drama is structured by "case&nbsp;
of the week" crimes that Bosch needs to solve.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.720
Simultaneously, it features overarching,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:55.440
season-long — and even series-long —&nbsp;
story arcs that weave in greater themes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.720
As the seasons progress, Connelly's other&nbsp;
"Bosch" books, of which there are over 20,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:06.640
are mined for story inspiration. The series&nbsp;
wrapped up its seventh and final season in 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:12.320
but fans didn't have to weep for long: The show&nbsp;
quickly earned a spinoff. Fans of "Longmire" are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:18.080
sure to like how "Bosch" intertwines characters,&nbsp;
individual episodes, and big-picture plots.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:24.480
If you've got a hankering for a real Western after&nbsp;
enjoying "Longmire," go back in time with "Hell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:32.320
on Wheels." This historical drama ran on AMC for&nbsp;
five seasons from 2011 to 2016. The series is set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:38.720
in the years after the American Civil War, and&nbsp;
stars Anson Mount as Cullen Bohannon, a former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:45.120
Confederate soldier who joins the Union Pacific&nbsp;
Railroad. Colm Meaney co-stars as Thomas "Doc"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:51.600
Durant, a real historical figure who invested in&nbsp;
the first transcontinental railroad. Common plays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:58.000
Elam Ferguson, a recently freed enslaved person&nbsp;
who becomes Cullen's assistant and bodyguard.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.800
The series, and the characters, move across&nbsp;
the country as the railroad is built.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:08.880
This allows for many procedural scenarios. The&nbsp;
laborers, surveyors, builders, sex workers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.960
and everyone else who travels along with&nbsp;
the encampment refer to themselves as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:17.360
"Hell on wheels," giving the show its&nbsp;
title. They're well worth getting to know.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:24.080
In AMC's "The Son," British actor Pierce Brosnan&nbsp;
heads to the American West. From that simple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:29.440
starting point, things get complicated, as "The&nbsp;
Son" likes to play with time. The main setting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:37.040
is 1917, where Brosnan plays Eli McCullough,&nbsp;
the iconic "First Son of Texas." He secures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:42.560
his legacy as a wealthy oil tycoon by killing,&nbsp;
threatening, and deceiving his way to the top.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.920
“In this life, if you don’t&nbsp;
move forward, you die.”

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:55.680
"The Son" also takes the viewer back to 1850,&nbsp;
where a young Eli, played by Jacob Lofland,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:01.280
learns the ways of the Comanche and becomes a&nbsp;
respected warrior. The show also jumps forward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:07.920
to 1988, where Eli's granddaughter Jeannie,&nbsp;
played by Lois Smith, uncovers family secrets.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:13.280
It's a pretty neat setup, and though AMC only gave&nbsp;
the show two seasons, it's still worth a watch.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:19.280
The FX action-drama "Sons of Anarchy" could&nbsp;
certainly fill the "Longmire" hole in your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.840
heart. The series follows the members of&nbsp;
an outlaw motorcycle club rooted in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:28.880
Central Valley of California. Charlie&nbsp;
Hunnam stars as Jackson "Jax" Teller,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:33.520
the vice president of the Sons of Anarchy&nbsp;
Motorcycle Club. He begins to question his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:38.640
role in the club after discovering the journals of&nbsp;
his deceased father, the club's former president.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:44.480
Throughout the series, the club is involved in&nbsp;
many illegal activities. So, while this series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:50.320
may be like "Longmire" in many respects, the long&nbsp;
arm of the law is considered the bad guy here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:55.680
always looking to shut them down and toss their&nbsp;
members in jail. The series also addresses racism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.880
in the world of outlaw motorcycle clubs, the&nbsp;
role of vigilantism, and government corruption.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:06.480
The Netflix series "Bloodline" begins with&nbsp;
John Rayburn's ominous voice. He says,

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:12.320
"Sometimes you know something's coming. You can&nbsp;
feel it. In the air. In your gut. And you don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:16.880
sleep at night. The voice in your head is telling&nbsp;
you that something is going to go terribly wrong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:21.280
and there's nothing you can do to stop it.&nbsp;
That's how I felt when my brother came home."

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.320
As you might guess from this intense introduction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:28.560
"Bloodline" is steeped in secrets,&nbsp;
crime, and tense reunions.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:34.080
The story follows the Rayburn siblings of the&nbsp;
Florida Keys when the aforementioned black sheep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:39.600
of the family returns from who-knows-where. His&nbsp;
presence causes enough tension to kill off the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:45.680
family patriarch. While "Longmire" might be set&nbsp;
out west, "Bloodline" offers up the same thrilling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:51.040
ambiance in a more paradisiacal atmosphere.&nbsp;
Come on in, the turquoise water is fine.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:56.800
HBO's "Deadwood" ran for three seasons in&nbsp;
the '00s, wrapping up years later with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:03.600
2019 movie. The show is a historical Western&nbsp;
set in Deadwood, South Dakota in the 1870s.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:09.040
Timothy Olyphant stars as Seth Bullock,&nbsp;
a sheriff-turned-hardware store owner.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:15.680
Ian McShane plays saloon owner Al Swearengen.&nbsp;
As Deadwood grows from a ramshackle spot into a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:22.480
blossoming town, South Dakota itself prepares for&nbsp;
a more official, law-abiding existence. That means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:28.400
cleaning up the rabble. Complex drama ensues,&nbsp;
weaving together episodic arcs and lengthier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:33.760
storylines involving government corruption,&nbsp;
loyalty, and the early days of American crime.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:37.840
"Deadwood" is well known for its sharp&nbsp;
writing and stellar performances. It has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:45.040
also become known for its incredible amount of&nbsp;
swearing. One report counts a total of 2,980&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:51.040
f-bombs dropped during the show's three&nbsp;
seasons, with one occurring every 1.56 seconds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:55.360
"Deadwood" offers up the Western&nbsp;
procedural ambiance "Longmire" fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:59.840
crave and a degree of profanity so&nbsp;
immense, it's almost awe-inspiring.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:05.520
Kevin Costner’s most recent western adventure&nbsp;
is a modern one called "Yellowstone,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:11.280
which makes its home on the Paramount Network. The&nbsp;
series follows the Dutton family, sixth-generation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:16.320
owners of the largest working ranch in the&nbsp;
country. Costner stars as the patriarch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:21.520
John Dutton. The drama hinges on outsiders'&nbsp;
attempts at gaining access to the Duttons'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:26.880
land, conflicts with the neighboring Native&nbsp;
reservation, and a whole lot of family secrets.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:33.360
The Dutton family features three grown kids:&nbsp;
Kayce, Jamie, and Beth. Their lives form much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:38.400
of the backbone of the series, encompassing&nbsp;
substance abuse, illicit relationships,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:44.000
and frustrated dreams. All in all, "Yellowstone"&nbsp;
is an emotional, exciting, and altogether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:49.440
engrossing drama with Western flair. In short,&nbsp;
perfect for anyone who loves "Longmire."

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:56.000
After starring in "Deadwood," Timothy Olyphant&nbsp;
travelled into the future some 130 years to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:03.520
star in FX's modern drama "Justified." He plays&nbsp;
Deputy U.S. Marshal Raylan Givens. After shooting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:08.480
a Miami mobster, Givens is transferred&nbsp;
to Kentucky, where he happens to be from.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:15.280
It's not a happy homecoming. Drama, violence,&nbsp;
secrets, and lies ensue — often tangled together.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:19.920
"Justified" ran for six seasons and was&nbsp;
critically acclaimed throughout its run.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:24.960
Walton Goggins' performance as Boyd Crowder,&nbsp;
a white supremacist preacher who heads up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:29.840
the area's criminal underground, earned&nbsp;
particular praise, among other stellar roles.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:35.280
“Justified" is based on author Elmore&nbsp;
Leonard's work, especially "Fire in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:41.040
the Hole." The success of "Justified" inspired&nbsp;
Leonard to write another Givens-centric novel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:46.000
"Raylan." The book came out in 2012,&nbsp;
shortly before Leonard's death in 2013.

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:52.000
Here's where we get a little international with&nbsp;
this list. "Tin Star" is a British crime drama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:57.040
that revolves around a London detective who's&nbsp;
tasked with becoming the police chief of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:02.400
Canadian town in the Rocky Mountains. It's&nbsp;
"Old West" meets "Old World" — not exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:08.560
a common combination, but, as it turns out,&nbsp;
a fascinating one. Tim Roth stars as James&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:13.920
"Jim" Worth, the detective who moves his&nbsp;
family to Canada to escape his troubled past.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:19.840
The weird thing about this show is that when&nbsp;
Jim drinks, he becomes his violent alter-ego,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:25.920
Jack Devlin. It's intense, surprisingly&nbsp;
fun, and a bit weird, all at the same time.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:31.520
Christina Hendricks co-stars as Elizabeth&nbsp;
Bradshaw, an executive with North Stream Oil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:36.480
the company that dominates the town. She&nbsp;
tries to balance Chief Worth's presence with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:42.800
the biker gangs, criminals, and oil workers&nbsp;
of the town. "Tin Star" spans three seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:47.840
which first aired on Sky Atlantic, then&nbsp;
moved to Amazon. Interestingly, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:53.920
Season 3 — or Series 3, as the Brits call it —&nbsp;
takes place back in Liverpool, England. This omits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:59.360
the Western feel of the show, but not to worry:&nbsp;
It still maintains its crime-thriller ambiance.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:04.480
While some of the shows on this list can get&nbsp;
pretty dark and dramatic, "Hap and Leonard"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:11.600
is one that embraces its humor. This mystery&nbsp;
crime drama stars James Purefoy as Hap Collins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:17.600
a blue-collar dude who's spent time in prison, as&nbsp;
well as Michael Kenneth Williams as Leonard Pine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:24.000
a Black, gay Vietnam veteran. Set in the&nbsp;
1980s, the series takes place in east Texas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.120
where Hap and Leonard team up&nbsp;
on a get-rich-quick scheme.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:32.640
Soon enough, they pull ex-wives, townsfolk,&nbsp;
other criminals, and lawmen into their fold.

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:38.560
The show was created by novelist Joe R. Lansdale&nbsp;
and is based on his "Hap and Leonard" novels.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:44.320
In many ways, it's unlike any other show on&nbsp;
this list, blending together comedy, grit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:48.640
lawlessness, and outright absurdity.&nbsp;
If you're longing for that "Longmire"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:53.760
attitude but you'd also like to crack a smile once&nbsp;
in a while, "Hap and Leonard" is a great choice.

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:55.440
“I do what I can.”

00:09:56.160 --> 00:10:01.600
We're going across the pond again for this next&nbsp;
entry. Though ITV's "Broadchurch" doesn't have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:06.720
the Western edge that "Longmire" does, its&nbsp;
fascinating portrait of a town in crisis will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:12.880
no doubt lure you in. The series is set in the&nbsp;
fictional English village of Broadchurch. Here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:19.200
detectives Alec Hardy, played by David Tennant,&nbsp;
and Ellie Miller, played by Olivia Coleman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:24.240
are forced to team up, despite the vast&nbsp;
difference in their personalities. Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:28.720
1 follows their journey as they attempt to&nbsp;
solve the enigmatic killing of a local boy.

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:35.120
Broadchurch being a small town, other townsfolk&nbsp;
soon become involved. Things grow more and more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:41.040
complex in Seasons 2 and 3, wrapping the&nbsp;
whole series up in a twisty, mysterious bow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:46.080
The setting of the show provides just as much&nbsp;
ambiance as the chilling crimes themselves. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:51.200
white cliffs, gray skies, and rough seas&nbsp;
are basically characters unto themselves.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:56.560
If the mystery aspect of "Longmire" drew you in,&nbsp;
you'll find "Broadchurch" downright addictive.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:01.440
We're staying in England for this next entry&nbsp;
— but can you blame us? The leading man is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:07.520
just that good. In the BBC One crime drama&nbsp;
"Luther," Idris Elba stars as John Luther,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:13.120
a police detective for the Serious Crime Unit,&nbsp;
which sounds silly, but is official. Luther often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:18.560
gets sucked into the crimes he investigates,&nbsp;
especially those of serial killer Alice Morgan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:24.640
played by Ruth Wilson. The two spend the majority&nbsp;
of the series as both nemeses and companions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:27.840
infusing this dark crime&nbsp;
thriller with electric tension.

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:33.360
Luther is technically a miniseries, with only&nbsp;
two to six episodes per season, making the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:38.400
five-season series totally bingeable. There was&nbsp;
supposed to be an American remake, but it fell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:44.160
apart back in 2017. There is still chatter about&nbsp;
a "Luther" movie, so you best get into it now!

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:50.240
Are you up for a little sci-fi-horror to go&nbsp;
along with your neo-Western? If so, SyFy's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:57.280
"Wynonna Earp" might be right up your alley. It&nbsp;
stars Melanie Scrofano as the titular character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:03.200
the great-great-granddaughter of legendary Old&nbsp;
West lawman Wyatt Earp. That legacy isn't all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:07.920
it's cracked up to be. She's haunted by the&nbsp;
outlaws her ancestor killed, who take the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:13.920
form of undead revenants. Luckily, on her 27th&nbsp;
birthday, she discovers that she's inherited the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:19.920
ability to send them back to Hell, with a little&nbsp;
help from "Peacemaker," her ancestor's magic gun.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:25.200
"Wynonna Earp" ran for four seasons&nbsp;
on SyFy before being canceled in 2021.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:28.080
Don't count it out just yet, though — the show's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:32.240
passionate fanbase is working overtime&nbsp;
to secure the future of "Wynonna Earp."

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:36.800
If you're short on time and looking for&nbsp;
a single-season miniseries to binge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:43.520
check out Netflix's "Godless." Set in 1884,&nbsp;
"Godless" begins when young outlaw Roy Goode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:48.320
played by Jack O'Connell, runs out&nbsp;
on his cruel mentor. He soon stumbles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:53.520
onto La Belle, New Mexico, a town run&nbsp;
and populated almost entirely by women.

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:57.440
As it turns out, most of the men of&nbsp;
La Belle died in a mining accident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:03.280
leaving the town's women to run it as they&nbsp;
please. Jeff Daniels also stars as Frank Griffin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:08.400
the venomous outlaw Goode flees from. The&nbsp;
miniseries was a hit, earning its cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:13.200
and crew a handful of Emmy Awards and a&nbsp;
place on multiple best-of-the-year lists.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:18.160
Banshee captures neo-Western style&nbsp;
much like "Longmire" does, with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:25.040
major geographical twist. Set in Pennsylvania&nbsp;
Amish Country, "Banshee" stars Antony Starr&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:30.640
as an ex-con who assumes the identity of the&nbsp;
town's incoming sheriff, to hide from a powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:36.640
crime lord called Mr. Rabbit. When the sheriff&nbsp;
is killed, the ex-con, whose name we never learn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:42.160
swipes his identity and shows up in Banshee,&nbsp;
PA masquerading as the town's new lawman.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:46.080
"Banshee" earned mixed&nbsp;
reviews. Some watchers love it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:50.400
while others criticize its intense&nbsp;
violence and gratuitous sex scenes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:55.360
So yeah, it's a bit more wild than "Longmire,"&nbsp;
but it still utilizes that same gritty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.360 --> 00:14:00.800
procedural style in a unique setting. The show&nbsp;
ran for four seasons on Cinemax and definitely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:06.240
lives up to the lurid nature of that network's&nbsp;
reputation. It’s at least worth checking out.

